2 ADDR
1 OCCU 1523 Biskop Iver Muncks Kansler, 1537 kannik, 1537 St. Peters K. i Ribe, 1537 præst  Sct.Cathrine kirke i Ribe, Domherre (Ribe), , Var Kansler for Biskop Iver Munk, kannik, embedsmand, sognepræst og student fra universitetet i Köl
2 CONC n.
1 TITL Kansler
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 
2 CONT Jens Christiernsen Varder (ca. 1490/1495–1546/1548) var en dansk gejstlig, kansler for biskop Iver Munk i Ribe (1523) og sognepræst, kendt for sin deltagelse i forberedelsen af den danske kirkeordinans i 1537.
2 CONT **
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. c. 1537 [St. Peters K. i Ribe (37)] Mag. Jens Christensen Warde el. Warder, f. Varde c. 00; F. C. Nielsen, Bgmstr. i Varde; vist St. Køln 15; Biskop Iver Muncks Kansler 23; Kannik c. 37; ~ 40 . . . . . ; vist u. B.; [† 25/6 154
2 CONC 7; havde en Dtr., Karen, længe før sit Ægteskab, f. c. 25, b. 1/4 70, (see I. I. Hemmet i V. Vedsted)].
2 CONT
2 CONT PT 11:3 (1942), s. 189; Hegelund I s. 61, II s. 37; Kinch II, s. 16, 70-71, 190, 233, 794-795.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://wiberg-net.dk/916-17-Ribe.Cathr.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT * 
2 CONT
2 CONT Født omkring 1490 i Varde, som søn af borgmesteren i Varde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens var far til bl.a. Karen Jensdatter Varder (ca. 1525), men navnet på Karens mor kendes desværre ikke. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens var præst, katolsk naturligvis, for han indledte sin karriere før reformationen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Det betød samtidig, at han ikke giftede sig før omkring 1540, hvilket vil sige ca. 4 år efter reformationen (en katolsk præst må jo ikke gifte sig).
2 CONT
2 CONT Desværre kender vi ikke hustruens identitet, ligesom vi heller ikke ved, om det var den samme kvinde, som var mor til Karen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Men nu har vi jo set, at datteren Karen blev født omkring 1525, så hun blev altså født udenfor ægteskab som datter af en katolsk præst og en mor, vi ikke ved, hvem var. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Det fremgår bl.a. af ”Slægtebog over Afkommet af Borgmester Christjern Nielsen i Varde (omtr. 1500)” fra 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Christiansen Varder skulle være identisk med den Jens Christiansen, som i 1516 blev indskrevet ved Universitetet i Køln, og som i 1523 var biskop Iver Muncks Kansler, var præst ved Sct. Peders Kirke og medlem af Domkapitlet. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Således deltog han 1537 som udsending for dette i en forsamling af gejstlige, som kongen havde ladet sammentræde i Odense, hvor de lavede det udkast til en kirkeordinans, som senere i det væsentligste blev fulgt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ifølge Ole Degns "Rig og fattig i Ribe" døde '''Jens Christensen Varder.'''  1547 i Ribe.  Han var sognepræst ved Sct.  Kathrine kirken i Ribe, ca. 1537-47, mag..  Skatmester 1549,1552,1562,1563, FM (Medl. af de 24 mænd) 1551...71
2 CONC ,pengemester 1571-72,1583-84, Gilde. forstander. 1589-92. Han var  søn af Christjern Nielsen, borgmester i Varde, 
2 CONT
2 CONT J. Kinck Ribe bys historie bind 2 p. 70
2 CONT
2 CONT Den første Sognepræst ved St. Kathrine Kirke var M. '''Jens Kristjernsen Varder,''' om hvem den gamle Kathrine Skolebog har Følgende: „Han var fulgt efter M. Hans Markorsen i Præsteæmbedet ved St. Peders Sogn. Da dernæst Religions
2 CONC forandringen nærmede sig, og Kirkerne på flere Steder (,,passim") nedreves, og Sognene sammenlagdes, blev han selv valgt til den første Sognepræst ved det nye St. Kathrine Sogn omtrent 1537, efter at Munkene (i Sortebrødre-Kloster
2 CONC et) vare blevne fordrevne. Han døde år 1547 på St. Knuds Dag, som er den 25de Juni. Han tjente altså i 10 år i Præsteæmbedet ved hin Kirke. I Ægteskab levede han kun 7 Ar." — Han skal have været en Søn af Borgmester''' Kristiern N
2 CONC ielsen''' i Varde. Det er muligvis ham, som 1516 indskreves ved Universitetet i Køln, og som 1523 var Biskop Iver Muncks Kansler. Præst ved St. Peders Kirke blev han vist kort før Reformationen, og omtrent på samme Tid blev han Me
2 CONC dlem af Kapitlet. Tilligemed M. Søren Olufsen NeLb repræsenterede han dette på Mødet i Odense i Begyndelsen af 1537. 3 Ar senere giftede han sig; men som så mange katholske Gejstlige havde han allerede langt tidligere en Datter; d
2 CONC et er vel dertil, den gamle Skolebog hentyder ved sin Bemærkning om, at han kun levede 7 Ar i Ægteskab. Hans''' Datter, Karen,''' blev først gift med en '''Jens i Ribe''', derpå med Borg, mester '''Lavrids Tøgersen''' sammesteds.^
2 CONC ) — M.  '''Jens Kristiernsen''' var tillige forlenet med hellig Korses Vikarie i Vejle, som efter hans Død blev tillagt Hospitalet i Ribe, Han havde idet mindste 2 Søstre, af hvilke ''' Kirsten''' var gift første gang med Borgmest
2 CONC er '''Mads Nielsen i Vejle,''' Faderen til Biskop '''Jakob Madsen Vejle''', andengang med '''Klemen Sørensen,''' ligeledes Borgmester i Vejle, af  Fødsel en Riber. Den anden Søster,''' Mette''', var gift med Rådmand '''Lavge Steff
2 CONC ensen''' i Ribe og således Moder til Biskop '''Hans Lavgesen'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT J. Kinck Ribe Bys historie bind 2. p 16 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Kristjernsen Varder Deltog i den Forsamling af Gejstlige, som Kongen i Begyndelsen af 1537 lod sammentræde i Odense, og som der forfattede det Udkast til en '''Kirkeordinans,''' som senere i det Væsentlige blev fulgt. Også Ud
2 CONC sendinge fra Domkapitlerne havde deltaget i dette Møde; således på Ribe Kapitels Vegne M. Søren Neb og M. '''Jens Kristjernsen Varder''', af hvilke den Sidste tillige var Sognepræst ved St. Peders (senere ved St. Kathrine) Kirke. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ***
2 CONT
2 CONT Born around 1490 in Varde, as the son of the mayor of Varde.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens was the father of, among others, Karen Jensdatter Varder (around 1525), but the name of Karen's mother is unfortunately not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens was a priest, a Catholic of course, because he began his career before the Reformation.
2 CONT
2 CONT This also meant that he did not marry until around 1540, which is about 4 years after the Reformation (a Catholic priest is not allowed to marry).
2 CONT
2 CONT Unfortunately, we do not know the identity of his wife, nor do we know whether it was the same woman who was Karen's mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT But now we have seen that the daughter Karen was born around 1525, so she was born out of wedlock as the daughter of a Catholic priest and a mother we do not know who was.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is evident from, among other things, the “Genealogy of the Descendants of Mayor Christjern Nielsen in Varde (around 1500)” from 1879.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Christiansen Varder was supposed to be identical with the Jens Christiansen who was enrolled at the University of Cologne in 1516, and who in 1523 was Bishop Iver Munck's Chancellor, was a priest at St. Peter's Church and a m
2 CONC ember of the Cathedral Chapter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thus, in 1537, he participated as an envoy for this in an assembly of clergy that the king had summoned in Odense, where they drafted a church ordinance that was later essentially followed.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Ole Degn's "Rig og fattig i Ribe" Jens Christensen Varder died. 1547 in Ribe. He was parish priest at Sct. Kathrine church in Ribe, ca. 1537-47, mag.. Treasurer 1549,1552,1562,1563, FM (Medl. of the 24 men) 1551...71,
2 CONC  money master 1571-72,1583-84, Gilde. superintendent. 1589-92. He was the son of Christjern Nielsen, mayor of Varde,
2 CONT
2 CONT J. Kinck Ribe bys historie vol. 2 p. 70
2 CONT
2 CONT The first parish priest at St. Kathrine Church was M. Jens Kristjernsen Varder, about whom the old Kathrine School Book has the following: "He had followed M. Hans Markorsen in the priesthood at St. Peders Parish. When the religio
2 CONC us change approached, and the churches in several places ("passim") were demolished, and the parishes were merged, he himself was elected the first parish priest at the new St. Kathrine Parish around 1537, after the monks (in the 
2 CONC Black Brothers Monastery) had been expelled. He died in 1547 on St. Knud's Day,
2 CONT
2 CONT which is the 25th of June. He served for 10 years in the priesthood at that church. He lived in marriage only 7 years." — He is said to have been a son of Mayor Kristiern Nielsen in Varde. It is possibly he who was enrolled at the
2 CONC  University of Cologne in 1516, and who in 1523 was Bishop Iver Munck's Chancellor. He was shown to be a priest at St. Peter's Church shortly before the Reformation, and at about the same time he became a member of the chapter. He
2 CONC  also represented this, together with M. Søren Olufsen NeLb, at the meeting in Odense in the beginning of 1537. 3 years later he married; but like so many Catholic clergymen he had a daughter much earlier; it is probably to this t
2 CONC hat the old school book alludes by its remark that he only lived 7 years in marriage. His daughter, Karen, was first married to a Jens in Ribe, then to Borg, master Lavrids Tøgersen of the same place.^) — M. Jens Kristiernsen was 
2 CONC also endowed with the Vicarage of the Holy Cross in Vejle, which after his death was assigned to the Hospital in Ribe. He had at least 2 sisters, of whom Kirsten was married first to Mayor Mads Nielsen in Vejle, the father of Mayo
2 CONC r Mads Nielsen of Vejle, father of Bishop Jakob Madsen of Vejle, second time with Klemen Sørensen, also Mayor of Vejle, by birth a Riber. The other sister, Mette, was married to Councilman Lavge Steffensen of Ribe and thus mother 
2 CONC of Bishop Hans Lavgesen.
2 CONT
2 CONT J. Kinck Ribe City History volume 2. p 16
2 CONT
2 CONT Jens Kristjernsen Varder participated in the assembly of clergy that the King had convened in Odense at the beginning of 1537, and that there drafted a church ordinance that was later essentially followed. Delegates from the cathe
2 CONC dral chapters also participated in this meeting; thus on behalf of the Ribe Chapter, M. Søren Neb and M. Jens Kristjernsen Varder, of whom the latter was also parish priest at St. Peders (later at St. Kathrine) Church.
