1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Godager søndre (Gnr. 94, bnr. 1)
2 CONT
2 CONT Godager with underlying Otten sæter to Sheriff Erik Lange (for 640 rdr.), which by deed 16 November 1712 with Otten sæter sells Godager to Jacob Isaksen Cold (1677-1730) and wife Karen Jensdtr. for 1200 rdr.
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 April 1720, Jacob Cold leases Husehagen o. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1723 the land register, Jacob Cold owner and user of Godager søndre. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Cold mortgages Godager søndre on 31  March 1730 to his brother Johan Cold for 700 rdr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At the Thing 23 / 9 1735 was the description stated that Godager søndre is lagting farm since 1712. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Karen Jensdatter, Jacob Colds widow is old. It proposed a tax Godager søndre of 2 skill. pr. full farm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 November 1743 Godager søndre farm with Otten sæter sold by auction by Magistrate Hieronymus Jensen and prosten Johan Cold to lensmann Lars Nilsson Veflingstad, who on 22 November 1743 secured after Johan Cold for 800 rdr.
