1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hans Luder married''' Margarethe Lindemann''' of the same age around 1479 (* 1459 in Neustadt an der Saale , † June 30, 1531 in Eisleben). Margarethe, also known as Hanna in the family, came from the Lindemann midd
2 CONC le-class family in Eisenach. The Lindemanns came from the upscale artisan or merchant class; Margaret's brothers had completed law studies, a prerequisite for further social advancement. Another branch of the Lindemann family was 
2 CONC involved in mining and metallurgy: '''Margarethe's uncle, Antonius Lindemann,''' was at that time the highest mountain administrator (count) in the county of Mansfeld. Both components explain the marriage of Hans Luder, who comes 
2 CONC from the village's upper class, to a woman from the urban middle class.
2 CONT
