2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lindemann (noble family)''':
2 CONT
2 CONT Coat of arms of the noble family von Lindeman after the renewal of the noble title in 1784:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The original bourgeois family Lindemann with the ancestor Johannes Lindemann from Neustadt an der Saale was Elector Augustus already in 1563 with the Saxon Councilor, Vice-Chancellor and Privy Council, Lawrence Lindemann ( 1520
2 CONC  - 1585 )''', inheritance, reclining and court gentleman on Sedlitz in the hereditary nobility. The '''title of nobility was only used by a few family members, most of whom continued to call themselves Lindemann''' . The family wa
2 CONC s related to Martin Luther through the daughter of Johannes Lindemann, Margarethe Lindemann .
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Individual Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT Student in Erfurt, immatrikuliert 1511 in Leipzig, 1512 Baccalaureus, 09 NOV 1519 Magister der Universitait Wittenberg, dann Schulmeister in Schleusingen, 1529 Rektor der Lateinschule in Schweinfurt, 1530 Flucht nach Mansfeld zu L
2 CONC uthers Eltern, 1535 Schulmeister in Ohrdruff, am 11 MAY 1541 ordiniert in Wittenberg, durch Bugenhagen Pfarrer in Auerbach/Vogtl. von 1541-1547, anschlieÃend Superintendent in Schweinfurt.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Verheiratet war Johannes Lindemann''' zweimal in Schleusingen''' und in '''dritter Ehe mit Margarethe N. N'''. (wiederverheiratete Sporer), die vermutlich aus Auerbach im Vogtland stammte.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sein älterer Sohn Philipp Lindemann starb 1563 bei einem Reitunfall bei Ingolstadt ohne Nachkommen. Sein 1547 geborener''' jüngster Sohn Johannes wurde Schulmeister im erzgebirgischen Bockau und starb dort am 30. Oktober 1621'''. 
2 CONC Er hinterließ eine zahlreiche Nachkommenschaft.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Lindemann_(Theologe)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.schweinfurtfuehrer.de/pers%C3%B6nlichkeiten/bedeutende-b%C3%BCrgerinnen-und-b%C3%BCrger-der-freien-reichsstadt-schweinfurt/johann-lindemann/
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Lindemann 1493-1554 Marriage: 1524 Schweinfurt Bayern Deutschland Margarethe Sporerin, 1488-1554
2 CONT
2 CONT Children (5) i. Anna Lindemann, 1525-1589
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Philipp Lindemann, 1535-1563
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Salome Lindemann, 1538-1608
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.  Anna Maria Elisabeth Lindemann, 1545-
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Johannes Lindemann Jr., 1547-1621
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/9W13-WGS/caspar-adam-lindemann-1346
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes Lindemann''' (1488–1554), Magister zu Wittenberg, Pfarrer und Superintendent zu Auerbach (Vogtland) ∞ 1.''' Catharina geb. Sporer''' (1488–vor 1545), 2. '''Margarethe geb. Sporer''' († 1554)
2 CONT
2 CONT a. Anna Lindemann (1525–1589) ∞ 1546 Paulus Dolwitzer, († 1571), Konrektor in Zwickau, 10 Kinder, davon 5 Söhne
2 CONT
2 CONT b. Salome Lindemann (1531–1608)
2 CONT
2 CONT c. Philipp Lindemann (1532–1563), Magister
2 CONT
2 CONT d. Barbara Lindemann († 1564)
2 CONT
2 CONT e. Elisabeth Lindemann (1545–1598)
2 CONT
2 CONT f.Johannes Lindemann (1547–1621), Schulmeister zu Bockau ∞ Margarethe N. (1548–1611)
2 CONT   f.1 Johannes Lindemann se seun: Reinhardt Lindemann (1582–nach 1634)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.stadtwikidd.de/wiki/Lindemann_(Adelsgeschlecht)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Es bleibt der dritte Bruder von Martin Luthers Mutter, der '''David Lindemann''' Er ist entweder in Neustadt geblieben oder von Eisenach in seinen Geburtsort zurückgekehrt. Dort wird 1488 der erste Sohn Johann Lindemann geboren, b
2 CONC enannt wie zu dieser Zeit üblich nach dem Großvater. Das ist der '''Johann Lindemann''', der dann als''' Pfarrer in Auerbach''' wirkt. Unser Auerbacher Pfarrer ist also auch ein''' Cousin des Reformators''', ein Verwandter Martin 
2 CONC Luthers mütterlicherseits.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archiv-auerbach.de/pdf/Elke%20u.%20Hilmar%20Jantke%20-%20Johann%20Lindemann.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ======================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria ist das achte Kind des Bockauer Schindelmachers Baltzer PÜSCHEL (KEKULÉ-Nr. 2050, ~ 15.08.1590 in Bockau/ Sachsen - † Nach 1637 in Bockau) und der Susanna LINDEMANN (KEKULÉ -Nr. 2051, * 29.03.1594 in Bockau - † nicht bekannt
2 CONC ). Beide haben am 04.05.1617 in Bockau geheiratet. Die Susanna LINDEMANN ist das vierte Kind des Schulmeisters zu Bockau und Aue (Sachsen), '''Johannes LINDEMANN''' (KEKULÉ -Nr. 4102, * err. 1547 in Auerbach/ Vogtland - † 30.10.16
2 CONC 21 in Bockau), und der '''Magdalena''' (KEKULÉ -Nr. 4103, Herkunft nicht bekannt, † 01.05.1611 in Bockau). Johannes ist der Sohn des J'''ohann LINDEMANN''' (KEKULÉ -Nr. 8204, * 1488 in '''Bad Neustadt/ Fränk. Saale/ Franken''' - †
2 CONC  18.04.1554 in Schweinfurt/ Franken).''' Er wird erwähnt als "Johann zur Neustatt an (auch vor) der Rhene" und ist Magister der Universität zu Wittenberg sowie Prediger der Reformation und Superintendent in Schweinfurt.''' Seine F
2 CONC rau ist die''' Margarethe SPORER''' in (vermutlich aus Auerbach/ Vogtland, weitere Angaben nicht bekannt). Der Vater des "Johann zur Neustatt an der Rhene" ist der Bürger in Neustadt a. d. Saale, David LINDEMANN (KEKULÉ -Nr. 16408
2 CONC , * um 1456-60 in Bad Neustadt an der Saale - † nicht bekannt), seine Ehefrau ist nicht bekannt. Davids Schwester, Margaretha LINDEMANN (* um 1460 - † 30.06.1531), heiratet 1479 in Eisenach den Bergmann u. Schieferhauer Hannß LUDE
2 CONC R (* err. 1459 in Möhra/ Eisenach - † 05.06.1530 in Mansfeld)
2 CONT . Am 10.11.1483 wird den Eheleuten LUDER als zweiter Sohn der spätere Kirchenreformator, Doktor der Theologie und Professor zu Wittenberg, Martin LUTHER in Eisleben geboren. Vgl. auch Stammtafel Familie LUTHER Möhraer Linie, Stamm
2 CONC linie von Joachim LUTHER
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Die Ahnenlisten der Ahnenforschung Krauß © 2003-2015
2 CONT
2 CONT https://michael-kraus.hpage.com/get_file.php?id=32117223&vnr=458586
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Margarethe SPORER''' in, weiteres nicht bekannt; vermutlich aus Auerbach (Vogtland); vermutlich römisch-katholisch. Möglicherweise nach dem Tod Johann LINDEMANNs wiederverheiratete SPORER. oo um 1545 in Auerbach (Vogtland) '''J
2 CONC ohann LINDEMANN'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Quelle: Ahnengemeinschaft mit Wolfgang LIEBEHENSCHEL, Berlin (2. Vorstand der Lutheridenvereinigung e. V.) Kinder:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Elisabeth, * err. 1545, ▭ 06.05.1598 in Stangengrün, oo Caspar DROMMER, * um 1540 in Auerbach (Vogtland), ▭ 07.03.1611 in Stangengrün, 1574 Bürgermeister in Auerbach (Vogtland), 1596-1611 Schulmeister in Schönheide, 1579-1583 Ra
2 CONC tsgeschworener in Auerbach (Vogtland) Kinder: Catharina; Barbara; Maria; Magdalena, oo 21.05.1599 in Stangengrün Christoph KRÖTZSCH aus Wildenau; Jacob, * 1581, ▭ 29.06.1640, 59 Jahre (Quelle u. a.: Stangengrün-Genealogische Entwi
2 CONC cklung einer Bauerngemeinde im Kreis Zwickau/ Sachsen 1460-1800 von Johannes GÜNDEL, S.
2 CONT
2 CONT ======================================================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Lindemann_(Theologe)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann Lindemann (theologian)''':
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann (also Johannes ) Lindemann''' (* 1488 in Neustadt an der Saale , † April 18, 1554 in Schweinfurt ) was a '''German teacher and Protestant theologian''' .
2 CONT
2 CONT Life:
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johann Lindemann, a cousin of Martin Luther, was the son of David Lindemann, a citizen of Neustadt an der Saale. Johann Lindemann came from an old middle-class family from Eisenach , his great-grandfather Hans Lindemann acquire
2 CONC d there in 1406 , the civil rights .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT About childhood and youth Lindemann's is not known, most likely he has as a member of the middle class , a school attended. He studied at the University of Leipzig in 1511 and became a baccalaureate there in 1512 . He has been a m
2 CONC aster of the University of Wittenberg since November 1519 . Afterwards he was schoolmaster in Schleusingen , where''' he married around 1520 .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Peasants' War he stayed in his hometown Neustadt an der Saale , probably as a teacher or preacher . Here Lindemann and the theologian Andres was on 30 May 1525 by the leaders of the Houses heap in writing and under the 
2 CONC guarantee of safe conduct by the Council of the allied with the rebellious peasants and craftsmen town to the arbitration of differing interpretations of the evangelical faith within the Bauer pile requested. There were two opposi
2 CONC ng political -religious groups formed: first, a reformatory -gemäßigte and the other one under the influence of the teachings of Thomas Müntzer standing social revolutionary - radical . The leaders of the crowd feared turmoil . Th
2 CONC e cause was the sermon by the leader of the Thuringian Baptist movement Hans Römer . As a supporter and former fighter of Müntzer, Römer incited the stately houses in her camp after the lost battle at Frankenhausen , the authoriti
2 CONC es with the sword to destroy and shed their blood.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Peasant War '''Lindemann became a teacher at the Latin school in Schleusingen and married there for the'''''' second time'''. In '''1529 he was appointed rector of the Latin School in Schweinfurt.''' Here he taught Luthe
2 CONC r's Little Catechism and was therefore reported by " papists " to Konrad II von Thüngen , the Prince-Bishop of Würzburg . Konrad, notorious for the cruel punishment of religious opponents, then sent an armed squad of two hundred m
2 CONC en against Schweinfurt to " arrest the thor " to have Lindemann arrested. From the captainWarned of the squad beforehand, Lindemann escaped with the help of a servant and fled to the Thuringian Forest in spring 1529, equipped by t
2 CONC he said captain with high shoes, half a guilder and a gag skewer . In the summer of 1529 he helped a charcoal burner at work in the Thuringian Forest and thus made a living.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He became emaciated during the winter 1529/ 30 Luther's parents to Mansfeld''' , where he - at first not recognized by these - first, a pittance of bread and some food was given. The Lutherans welcomed him into their house. In 
2 CONC the spring of 1530, on the advice of''' Hans Luther''' , Lindemann took the job of a hut clerk in Mansfeld, but he gave it up again in 1531 because of the godless behavior of the miners . '''His son Philipp Lindemann was born in M
2 CONC ansfeld around 1533 - 1535 , who in 1554 as a master and from 1559 as Professor at the University of Wittenberg is demonstrable.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes Lindemann was a teacher in Ohrdruf until 1541 . That same year he was Johannes Bugenhagen in Wittenberg ordained and after a successful petition Lindemanns to Martin Luther through the mediation of priest in Auerbach in V
2 CONC ogtland appointed. During the Schmalkaldic War , Lindemann lost his extensive library and all his belongings in the event of an attack by Bohemian troops , had to leave Auerbach and stayed with his''' cousin Cyriacus Lindemann''' 
2 CONC , then principal of the Fürstenschule Pforta . Around 1546 he became a '''pastor in Zwickau''' Through his friend Philipp Melanchthon , after initial hesitation,''' Lindemann became a pastor and superintendent in''' '''Schweinfurt
2 CONC  in 1547''' . Here it was Lindemann's special merit to counteract the provisions of the interim with which the Reformation was to be pushed back. He also made the acquaintance of from Schweinfurt Italy coming humanist Olympia Mora
2 CONC ta , who see him as strong character , describing fixed in the Protestant faith man.
2 CONT
2 CONT In a letter from Mayor and Council of the City of Schweinfurt to Sutellius from 1547, Johann Lindemann was mentioned as a learned man with respectable Christian good manners and conduct, whose sermons probably left a deep impressi
2 CONC on on his listeners.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''He died in 1554 during the Second Margrave War''' during the siege and bombardment of the Imperial City of Schweinfurt by federal troops. His place of work, the St. Johannis church , was badly damaged. He left at least six chil
2 CONC dren.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Johannes Lindemann was married twice in Schleusingen and in a third marriage to Margarethe NN (remarried Sporer), who probably came from Auerbach in the Vogtland .'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''His older son Philipp Lindemann died in 1563 in a riding accident near Ingolstadt without descendants.''' His youngest son '''Johannes, born in 1547, became schoolmaster in Bockau''' in the Ore Mountains and died there on Octob
2 CONC er 30, 1621 . He left numerous offspring .
2 CONT
