1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hans Nicolai Lange (2 December 1795 – 24 December 1848) was a Norwegian priest and politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Jevnaker to Johan Jørgen Lange and Dorothea Helena Larsen, he was the older brother of politicians Otto Vincent and Ulrik Frederik Lange, brother-in-law of Nils Landmark and Even Hanssen and uncle of Johan Jørgen Lange Han
2 CONC ssen.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1825 he married Anna Rebecca Blix. They had no children.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was elected to the Norwegian Parliament in 1839, while working as a church teacher in Drammen. He later became vicar in Bragernes parish, and was also mayor of Drammen for some time.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1848 in Paris, France due to ill health.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Nicolai Lange (1795 - 1848), kateket og førstelærer ved Bragernes borgerskole (1828 - 46), sogneprest til Bragernes (1846 - 48) ordfører (1842 - 47).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Ministerialbok===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Døde og begravede menn 1849, Buskerud fylke, Bragernes, Ministerialbok nr. II 2 (1848-1859), side 288. Permanent sidelenke: [http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:kb_read?idx_kildeid=1065&idx_id=1065&uid=ny&idx_side=-286 Hans Nicolai La
2 CONC nge] - begravede 8 mai 1848 - Bragernes
