1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was elected to the Norwegian Parliament in 1842 and 1845, while working as a headmaster in Tromsøe.[1] He was then elected three more times, in 1854, 1857 and 1859, from the constituency Lillehammer og Hamar. He
2 CONC  worked as a school principal there.[1] He was also mayor for some time.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Jevnaker to Johan Jørgen Lange and Dorothea Helena Larsen,[2] he was the younger brother of politicians Hans Nicolai and Otto Vincent Lange,[3] brother-in-law of Nils Landmark and Even Hanssen and uncle of Johan Jørgen Lan
2 CONC ge Hanssen.
2 CONT
2 CONT In March 1833 he married Stine Charlotte Cathrine Blix. They had seven children.[2] He died in 1878 in Lillehammer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ulrik Frederik J. Lange var første bestyrer for Tromsø middels- og realskole, som nå heter Kongsbakken videregående skole.  -  Fredrik Langes gate i Tromsø, Troms - har fått navnet etter Ulrik Frederik J. Lange.
