2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_S%C3%B8rensen_Vedel
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Sørensen Vedel (9 November 1542 – 13 February 1616) was a Danish priest and historiographer. He translated the Gesta Danorum by Saxo Grammaticus into Danish in 1575, and published the influential "Hundredvisebogen" in 1591.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders Sørensen was born in Vejle, from which place the Vedel name comes.14 years old he moved to study in Ribe, and after finishing his education he moved on to Copenhagen University in 1561. In 1562, he was the tutor of astronom
2 CONC er Tycho Brahe on Brahe's Grand Tour in Europe,forming a lasting bond of friendship with him.Vedel started studying at Wittenberg in 1565, which he finished in 1566, and was appointed priest at Copenhagen Castle in 1568. Vedel's h
2 CONC istorical knowledge was admired by leading politicians including Christoffer Valkendorf, Bjørn Andersen, Arild Huitfeldt Johan Friis and Peder Oxe, and he was seen as the right man to continue Christiern Pedersen's Danish language
2 CONC  translation of the Latin chronicle Gesta Danorum by Saxo Grammaticus.
2 CONT
2 CONT He started the translation work in 1570, and the finished work "Den danske Krønicke" was published in 1575. The work was both a translation and rewriting of the original Latin phrases. While working on the translation, he was give
2 CONC n the income of a canon at Ribe Cathedral in 1573. After pressure from Peder Oxe, Niels Kaas, and Jørgen Rosenkrantz, Vedel wrote a proposal for a Latin continuation of Saxo's work in 1578 which was finalized in 1581. He was relie
2 CONC ved of his priesthood in Copenhagen, and moved to Ribe in 1581.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was appointed Royal historiographer in 1584 and received a prelature at Ribe to support himself, and undertook the task of continuing the Danish chronicle in that year. However, he overreached himself in his attempt to do so. H
2 CONC e planned an ambitious work in twenty-two books dealing with both language and topography as well as with history. However other tasks, lack of help from secretaries, his own slowness and carefulness—and perhaps also a general und
2 CONC erestimation of the demands of this work—led to very modest results. In 1594, after the death of chancellor Niels Kaas, the task was given to Niels Krag, under Vedel's protestations. He got a one-year reprieve, but could not produ
2 CONC ce satisfactory results, after which he turned his work over to Niels Krag. Much of what he had written was lost at the fire of Copenhagen in 1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT One spin-off from this task which survived was his "Hundredvisebogen" (1591) of a hundred Danish ballads which became a solid foundation of later knowledge of the elder Danish literary tradition. It was published with the support 
2 CONC of Queen Sophie.[4] Vedel's own re-creation of some of the ballads shows his ability as a poet.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anders_S%C3%B8rensen_Vedel
2 CONT
2 CONT I Norge er han mest kjent som opphavsmann til «Hundreviseboka» (Et hundrede udvalgte danske viser), der han nedskrev middelalderballader og andre viser som var kjent i folketradisjonen. Hundreviseboka kom ut i 1591, og er den førs
2 CONC te i sitt slag i Nord-Europa. Vedels visesamling har vært et viktig referanseverk for norsk balladeforskning.
2 CONT
2 CONT I perioden 1570-75 oversatte han Saxos Gesta Danorum fra latin til dansk. Som historiker var han i gang med å samle materiale til en en stor danmarkshistorie, og nåede 22 bind før han måtte oppgi arbeidet.
2 CONT     * Biografi på Prosjekt Runeberg       
2 CONT     * Vedel på Kalliope
