1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ludvig Ludvigsen Munthe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Postgraduate/doctorand at Copenhagen University  '''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Steward and Tutor at the Royal Danish Court under King Fredrick II''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Canonicus and Arch Deacon of Lund Cathedral,'''
2 CONT
2 CONT At the death of his father Ludvig Munthe, he moved with his mother and brother ( Hans Ludvigsen Munthe) from Lubeck to Copenhagen to live with his sister who was wife of the Danish court preacher.  There the two boys became "page 
2 CONC stewards" (another source says "tutors") to the sons of Frederick II.   For extensive information about the Munthe family and their Belgium origins, go to http://aner.svaner.com/Generalogy/Ancestry/The_Munthes_eng.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT The following site gives additional information about his life (including the inscription on his grave site in a former chapel in Lund Cathedral).  http://kaspershus.se/phpgedview/individual.php?pid=I1613&ged=mintavla1.ged&tab=0
2 CONT
2 CONT http://kaspershus.se/phpgedview/family.php?famid=F773&ged=Precis_alla_2013-04-05.ged
2 CONT
2 CONT http://munthe.eu/Munthe_praster_kyrkor.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.nose.dk/Norge/paludan.html#7
