1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Holger Trolle played an important part during the Scanian War (1675-79) when Denmark tried to win back its eastern provinces from the Swedes. Trolle participated in all the major battles and he spent a lot of time 
2 CONC organising popular resistance and was responsible for some of the most able liaisons officers who organised the guerilla war against the Swedes (the snapphanar). He is mentioned as an able officer in Hirsch&Hirsch's "Fortegnelse o
2 CONC ver danske og norske officerer med flere 1648-1814". Hirsch & Hirsch claim he died in 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://finnholbek.dk/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I17736&tree=2
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT Ryegaard: https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ryeg%C3%A5rd
2 CONT
2 CONT *
